Package: delphir
Title: Structured Delphi and RAND/UCLA Analysis for Consensus Studies
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ming", "Yang", email = "yangpluszhu@sina.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Protocol-first toolkit for Delphi studies, RAND/UCLA
    appropriateness panels, and COMET core outcome set surveys.
    Locks consensus rules before analysis, summarises ordinal ratings
    with medians and agreement rates, classifies items, assesses
    between-round stability, prepares controlled feedback, generates
    multi-round Word/Excel questionnaires, screens first-round new items
    with a pre-specified dual pathway, and writes ACCORD, DCAT and
    CREDES aligned reports. RAND/UCLA panels use the manual panel-size
    table by default, with IPRAS, necessity ratings, two-round
    questionnaires and an optional Word report.
